  "final_message": "I haven't made the change, because the premise doesn't hold. `analytics-ingest` reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced`, and removing it would break that service.\n\n- **Required field:** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` calls `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. If `channel` is missing, the whole event is rejected with a `ContractViolationError`.\n- **Stored in reports:** `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes `channel` into the `orders` table. Its README (lines 23–31) documents `channel` (`web|store|marketplace`) as part of the contract.\n- **Effect:** once orders-service stops sending it, every new order would fail ingestion and drop out of analytics.\n\n`billing-service` appears to tolerate a missing `channel`. Its test at `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` passes `channel: undefined` without trouble. I didn't check its source.\n\nThe `analytics-ingest` checkout is read-only for me and belongs to another team. How do you want to proceed?\n\n1. **Coordinate first (safest):** the analytics team makes `channel` optional or drops it, then we remove it from orders-service.\n2. **Keep it on the event only:** remove it from the order model and API input, but keep sending it on `OrderPlaced`. Without the model field there'd be nothing to fill it from, so this probably isn't practical.\n3. **Remove it now:** I'd make the change in orders-service as asked and you'd handle the analytics breakage.\n\nIf you pick 1 or 3, the orders-service work touches these places:\n- `src/core/order.ts`\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- the tests and helpers\n- both `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, which have the `createApp` example",
